{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["T. S. Eliots father, who came from a prominent New England family, was on the Board of Directors of Washington University. He was also a Chairman at Hydraulic-Press Brick Company in St. Louis, a successful business man and a chemist. He married Eliots mother in 1868. What was her occupation?","A poet and a social worker"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"literature\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
